{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "nodeID": "42",
   "text": "Could global macro shocks overwhelm trade deals and push the U.S. trade deficit higher?",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "question",
   "toulmin": "framing",
   "oper": "framing",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#Q"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "43",
   "text": "They reflect demand, fiscal policy, currencies, and external adjustment—not just trade deals",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#P1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "44",
   "text": "The deficit rises unless stronger U.S. demand is matched abroad",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#P2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "45",
   "text": "Countries under pressure often rely on weaker currencies and exports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "stated_assumption",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.prior",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#P3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "46",
   "text": "Large external deficits mean weaker domestic demand and less global demand growth",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#D1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "47",
   "text": "EM weakness coincided with slower global trade and a larger U.S. non-oil deficit",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#D2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "48",
   "text": "Financial and political stress could weaken the euro",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#D3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "49",
   "text": "Domestic weakness plus dollar strength could create depreciation pressure",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#D4"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "50",
   "text": "Consumption-tax hikes have historically weakened domestic demand",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#D5"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "51",
   "text": "Europe, China, Japan, and EM demand all supported the global environment",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "evidence_data",
   "toulmin": "grounds",
   "oper": "grounds",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#D6"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "52",
   "text": "Lower domestic spending abroad reduces demand for imports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#M1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "53",
   "text": "Dollar strength hurts U.S. trade competitiveness",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#M2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "54",
   "text": "Strong U.S. demand plus weak foreign demand raises net imports",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "mechanism",
   "toulmin": "warrant",
   "oper": "warrant.mechanism",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#M3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "55",
   "text": "Foreign economies contribute less to import growth",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#C1"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "56",
   "text": "Currency shifts reinforce pressure on U.S. trade",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#C2"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "57",
   "text": "Foreign demand may no longer offset U.S. fiscal expansion",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "intermediate_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.step",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#C3"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "58",
   "text": "The U.S. trade deficit could rise even if the administration secures new trade agreements",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "main_claim",
   "toulmin": "claim",
   "oper": "claim.final",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#K"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "59",
   "text": "Argentina and Turkey are individually too small to drive the full outcome",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#X"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "60",
   "text": "Italy and China's eventual adjustments are not predetermined",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "caveat",
   "toulmin": "qualifier",
   "oper": "qualifier",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#QF"
  },
  {
   "nodeID": "61",
   "text": "Strong foreign demand could still counterbalance U.S. fiscal stimulus",
   "type": "I",
   "role": "counterpoint",
   "toulmin": "rebuttal",
   "oper": "rebuttal",
   "localID": "setser_jun_4_18#R1"
  },
